0,Teiwa language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teiwa_language,"Language family. Trans–New Guinea ? West Bomberai ?Teiwa is often classified as part of the Trans-New Guinea language family, but this is disputed. One reason is little lexical proof as well as the large geographical distance from the main island of New Guinea.",Teiwa,Trans-New Guinea
1,"Teiwa alphabet, prounciation and language",https://www.omniglot.com/writing/teiwa.htm,"Teiwa is a Trans-New Guinea language spoken on Pantar Island in the Alor archipelago in eastern Indonesia about about 4,000 people.The classification of Teiwa as a Trans-New Guinea language is disputed by some linguists.",Teiwa,Trans-New Guinea
