3,TEIWA - Rob Ruha with the New Zealand Symphony Orchestra ...Rob Ruha Goes Symphonic - RNZTeiwa language - WikipediaTeiwa - TransNewGuinea.orgPAPUA NEW GUINEA MUSIK HIST (Modern) - YouTubeTeiwa [Newguineaworld],https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WqSGettsxJI,"Dec 2, 2025 · Experience world class artistry, as Silver scroll-winning Māori artist Rob Ruha and the New Zealand Symphony Orchestra present ‘TEIWA’ at the Michael Fowler Centre – with special guests TOA (Te... Ruha will perform his own work ""Teiwa"" with the national orchestra and the eastern Bay of Plenty Kapa Haka ensemble, Te Taumata O Apanui. ""Teiwa"" is an abbreviated version of Hineteiwaiwa, a deity responsible for creating Māori performance art. Teiwa is often classified as part of the Trans-New Guinea language family, but this is disputed. One reason is little lexical proof as well as the large geographical distance from the main island of New Guinea. Also Known As: Tewa Deing. Sources: Stokhof (1975) Classification: Trans-New Guinea, West, Timor-Alor-Pantar, Alor-Pantar, Pantar. 'uuwad. Playlist ini menyediakan Musik dari Papua Nugini. There are three known dialects of Teiwa which are subclassified as follows: Deing-Teiwa Deing Sar-Teiwa Sar Teiwa",Teiwa,Trans-New Guinea
4,Teiwa - TransNewGuinea.org,https://www.transnewguinea.org/language/teiwa-deing,"Also Known As: Tewa Deing. Sources: Stokhof (1975) Classification: Trans-New Guinea, West, Timor-Alor-Pantar, Alor-Pantar, Pantar. 'uuwad.",Teiwa,Trans-New Guinea
5,database of the languages of New Guinea,https://transnewguinea.org/language/teiwa-lebang,"Information: Glottocode: leba1239 ISO 639: twe. Also Known As: Tewa Lebang. Sources: Stokhof (1975). Classification: Trans-New Guinea, West, Timor-Alor-Pantar, Alor-Pantar, Pantar. Map: Resources",Teiwa,Trans-New Guinea
6,"Teiwa Language (TWE) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/twe/,"Teiwa is a stable indigenous language of Indonesia. It belongs to the Trans-New Guinea language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.",Teiwa,Trans-New Guinea
7,Teiwa - twe (Trans-New Guinea) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/twe/,"Teiwa (twe) is part of the Trans-New Guinea family and Trans-New Guinea, West, Timor-Alor-Pantar, Alor-Pantar, Pantar class. Teiwa speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts",Teiwa,Trans-New Guinea
